GATK is required for callSNVs(criteria = "gatk").

GATK is not natively available on Windows. On Linux and macOS, install GATK
from https://gatk.broadinstitute.org/ and ensure the 'gatk' executable is
on your PATH, or pass its full path to callSNVs(gatk_path = "/path/to/gatk").

On Windows, use one of the following approaches:
  1. WSL2 (Windows Subsystem for Linux):
     https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/wsl/
     Install GATK inside WSL2 and run it manually. Note that Windows paths
     (e.g., D:/folder/file.bam) must be converted to WSL paths
     (e.g., /mnt/d/folder/file.bam).
  2. Docker:
     https://gatk.broadinstitute.org/hc/en-us/articles/360035889931-Docker
     Run the GATK Docker image and mount your data directory.

On Windows, callSNVs(criteria = "gatk") will stop with an informative error.
Use callSNVs(criteria = "fisher") or another method on Windows, or run GATK
manually via WSL2 or Docker.